{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEN41AbiwtAcweNoBtid","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The offline checks pass. Now I'll write ANSWER.md with the change, the open risk, and how to verify it from the usage log."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":835,"cache_read_input_tokens":34665,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":835},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f6036320-5761-49bf-a806-dd6950f24637","uuid":"e2eb87d1-9120-4f7a-bc3b-62f4d980d39d","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:33:42.020Z","request_id":"req_011CgEN3zrjn3b8e5W4xF79q"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEN41AbiwtAcweNoBtid","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CkUP2uhpmsc1EJKx84cD7j","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-Pri7dv/ANSWER.md","content":"# Answer: a memory write no longer evicts the static system prompt\n\n## Cause\n\n`build_system()` returned the whole system prompt as one text block with a single\n`cache_control` marker at the end. Caching is prefix-based, so any byte change\nafter the start of the block is a cache miss for everything. `save_fact` appends to\n`athlete.facts`, which is rendered inside that block, so each save changed the\nprefix and re-cached the ~1000-token instructions along with the facts. That\nmatches `NOTES.md` and the `usage.jsonl` pattern: `cache_read_input_tokens: 0` and\n`cache_creation_input_tokens` near the full prompt size on the call right after a save.\n\n## Change (`bot.py`, `build_system`)\n\nThe system prompt is now two text blocks, each with `cache_control: ephemeral`:\n\n1. `INSTRUCTIONS`: a constant, byte-stable across users and days.\n2. `athlete_context(a, today)`: the per-athlete tail (date, name, zones, goal,\n   facts, language).\n\nA `save_fact` now invalidates only block 2. Block 1 stays in cache.\n\nNothing else changed. Tools are still selected per message and placed above the\nsystem prompt, so a message that adds a tool group still misses the cache once.\nFact selection is still \"include all facts\", as before.\n\n## Checked offline\n\nStubbed `build_request` for two athletes on two days, with a fact added in between:\n\n- The instructions block is byte-identical in all three requests.\n- The tail changes after `save_fact`.\n- There are exactly two `cache_control` markers, which is within the limit of 4.\n\nI did not call the API. There is no `COACH_ANTHROPIC_KEY` in this environment, and I\ndid not deploy anything.\n\n## Open risk: the minimum cacheable length\n\nAnthropic only caches a prefix that is at least the model's minimum length\n(1024 tokens for Sonnet-class models). Here the first marker's prefix is the core\ntools plus `INSTRUCTIONS`. `INSTRUCTIONS` is about 2,480 characters, and the core\ntools are about 420 characters. From the existing `usage.jsonl` numbers, that prefix\nis probably just under 1024 tokens. If it is, the first marker is silently ignored,\nthe only effective marker is the tail one, and the bug is back: a memory write\nre-caches everything.\n\nI could not confirm this without an API call. To check:\n\n- After deploying, send a message and then a `save_fact` message within 5 minutes.\n  Then look at the next call in `logs/usage.jsonl`. If `cache_creation_input_tokens`\n  is roughly the tail size (~100-300 tokens), the fix works. If it is roughly the full\n  prompt (~1000+), the static block is below the minimum.\n- Or use the token-counting endpoint on the static prefix.\n\nIf it is below the minimum, the options are to lengthen the static block (only with\nuseful content, not filler) or to move a stable part of the per-athlete data into\nthe static block. I did not pad the prompt, because that would add tokens on every\ncache write without improving the answer.\n\n## Verify with the usage log\n\n- Two messages within 5 minutes: the second call's `cache_read_input_tokens` should\n  cover roughly the whole prompt.\n- After a `save_fact`: the next call's `cache_read_input_tokens` should be about the\n  static block, and `cache_creation_input_tokens` about the tail only.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":835,"cache_read_input_tokens":34665,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":835},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"par