mum cacheable length\n\nAnthropic only caches a prefix that is at least the model's minimum length\n(1024 tokens for Sonnet-class models). Here the first marker's prefix is the core\ntools plus `INSTRUCTIONS`. `INSTRUCTIONS` is about 2,480 characters, and the core\ntools are about 420 characters. From the existing `usage.jsonl` numbers, that prefix\nis probably just under 1024 tokens. If it is, the first marker is silently ignored,\nthe only effective marker is the tail one, and the bug is back: a memory write\nre-caches everything.\n\nI could not confirm this without an API call. To check:\n\n- After deploying, send a message and then a `save_fact` message within 5 minutes.\n  Then look at the next call in `logs/usage.jsonl`. If `cache_creation_input_tokens`\n  is roughly the tail size (~100-300 tokens), the fix works. If it is roughly the full\n  prompt (~1000+), the static block is below the minimum.\n- Or use the token-counting endpoint on the static prefix.\n\nIf it is below the minimum, the options are to lengthen the static block (only with\nuseful content, not filler) or to move a stable part of the per-athlete data into\nthe static block. I did not pad the prompt, because that would add tokens on every\ncache write without improving the answer.\n\n## Verify with the usage log\n\n- Two messages within 5 minutes: the second call's `cache_read_input_tokens` should\n  cover roughly the whole prompt.\n- After a `save_fact`: the next call's `cache_read_input_tokens` should be about the\n  static block, and `cache_creation_input_tokens` about the tail only.\n"}}}
